==================================================================================================
 (1) THE NONABELIAN EXPANDER: PSL_2(F_p), Ramanujan gap 2*sqrt(p) = Gauss-sum sqrt(p) arithmetic
==================================================================================================
    p |PSL_2(F_p)|=p(p^2-1)/2 Ramanujan gap 2sqrt(p) Gauss |g_p|=sqrt(p)
    3                     12                 3.4641             1.7321
    5                     60                 4.4721             2.2361
    7                    168                 5.2915             2.6458 <== apex7 = Aut(Fano)=GL_3(F_2)=168
   11                    660                 6.6332             3.3166
   13                   1092                 7.2111             3.6056
   23                   6072                 9.5917             4.7958
   31                  14880                11.1355             5.5678
  => the LPS Ramanujan expander on PSL_2(F_p) has spectral gap 2sqrt(p); the certificate is g_p=i sqrt(p).
     The expander's arithmetic = the Gauss-sum arithmetic. Apex-7: PSL_2(F_7)=Aut(Fano)=QR_7/octonion group.

==================================================================================================
 (2) SUM OF TWO SQUARES = p mod 4 = the Brouwer/Borsuk-Ulam (easy/hard) split
==================================================================================================
    p p mod4  sum of two squares? -1 QR mod p?    Gauss g_p           regime
    3      3                   NO        False      i*sqrt3 BORSUK-ULAM/hard
    5      1               (1, 2)         True   real sqrt5     BROUWER/easy
    7      3                   NO        False      i*sqrt7 BORSUK-ULAM/hard
   11      3                   NO        False     i*sqrt11 BORSUK-ULAM/hard
   13      1               (2, 3)         True  real sqrt13     BROUWER/easy
   17      1               (1, 4)         True  real sqrt17     BROUWER/easy
   19      3                   NO        False     i*sqrt19 BORSUK-ULAM/hard
   23      3                   NO        False     i*sqrt23 BORSUK-ULAM/hard
   31      3                   NO        False     i*sqrt31 BORSUK-ULAM/hard
  => p=1mod4 <=> sum of two squares <=> -1 is QR <=> Gauss real <=> BROUWER (easy). p=3mod4 <=> not a sum
     of two squares <=> Gauss imaginary i sqrt p <=> free Z_2 <=> BORSUK-ULAM (hard). apex 7 = the hard side.

==================================================================================================
 (3) FACILITY-LOCATION GAME: potential Phi = (6/7)^k - meas; PoA = optimum/adversarial
==================================================================================================
  OPTIMUM (equidistributed/independent, each runner safe w.p. 6/7): (6/7)^13 = 0.134801
  ADVERSARIAL min (extremizer): pentagon meas = 0.032261; sporadic = 0.032384
  POTENTIAL Phi(S) = (6/7)^k - meas(L_C): pentagon Phi = 0.102539 (the resonance penalty)
  PRICE OF ANARCHY = optimum / adversarial-min = 4.178  (pentagon binds)
  => meas(L_C) = (6/7)^k - Phi(S); Phi = the pairwise-resonance / additive-energy (Koksma-Hlawka
     discrepancy) the covering adversary induces. inf meas = (6/7)^k / PoA. Bounding PoA <= ~4.2 (i.e.
     Phi <= (6/7)^k(1-1/PoA)) gives inf meas >= (6/7)^k/PoA_max > 0 -- the potential-function lower bound.
  target 1/36=0.027778: extremizer/target = 1.161x (TIGHT); PoA to reach 1/36 = 4.853

==================================================================================================
 TANGENTIAL (owner's jumping-off): Pochhammer fiber, integer complexity, Hlawka-Koksma
==================================================================================================
  POCHHAMMER fiber fraction f(14) = (1/2)_12/(12)! = 0.161180 ~ 1/sqrt(pi*n)=0.150786
  INTEGER COMPLEXITY (Mahler-Popken): ||7||=6, ||14||=8, ||21||=9 (21=3*7 => ||21||<=||3||+||7||); tangential -- 'how hard to build the apex from 1s'.
  HLAWKA-KOKSMA: |meas(L_C) - (6/7)^k| <= V * D*  (variation x star-discrepancy of the runner phases) =
   the rigorous form of Phi(S) above: the adversary MAXIMIZES discrepancy D*(resonance), the covering
   constraint CAPS it => the PoA/potential bound is a Koksma-Hlawka discrepancy bound.
DONE.
